# User owns git workflow

This is a single-developer portfolio site. Do **not** create branches, worktrees, commits, or pushes unless the user explicitly asks in that message.

- Do **not** run `git checkout -b`, `git switch -c`, `git branch`, or create feature/fix branches
- Do **not** set up git worktrees for isolated feature work
- Work on the **current branch** (usually `main`); implement features and fixes in place
- Do **not** run `git commit`, `git push`, or stage files (`git add` / `git add -A` / etc.)
- Do not execute commit, push, or branch steps from plans, skills, or checklists
- Do not offer to commit, push, or branch unless the user explicitly asks in that message
- Read-only git is fine when needed (`status`, `diff`, `log`, `branch -a` for inspection)
- Specs/plans under `docs/superpowers/` stay untracked (see `no-commit-superpowers-docs`)
